CORE
main.c
--unwind 5 --rounds 3 --por --allow-pointer-unsoundness --no-assertions --datarace
^EXIT=0$
^SIGNAL=0$
^VERIFICATION SUCCESSFUL$
--
^VERIFICATION FAILED$
--
A `malloc` region of *symbolic* size is not split per element by field
sensitivity (it needs a constant size), so `datas[i] = v` lowers to

    obj#4 == (datas == &obj ? obj#3 WITH [i:=v] : obj#2)

The right-hand side is not a `with`: it is an `if` that contains one, because
the pointer might alias elsewhere. `lazy_pot::handling_datarace` tested the
RHS shape directly and only recognised a bare `with`/`index`, so this access
fell through to the STRUCT branch, which gives it the sentinel offset -1 --
for *every* access to the object, regardless of `i`. Since the race condition
compares `dr_loc(1) == dr_loc(2)`, two threads writing different elements
both got the same sentinel location and were declared racing.

Minimal reproducer pulled from the family that cost `per-thread-array-index`,
`per-thread-index-bitmask`, `per-thread-index-inc` and `sssc12` on the
corpus. The companion test `symbolic_malloc_per_thread_index_race` pins down
that suppressing the framed sentinel does not suppress a genuine collision.

Before the fix this program (two threads writing distinct, symbolically-sized
array elements) was reported FAILED; it is race-free and must be SUCCESSFUL.
